{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final","id":1139821,"title":"C20 changes from backer to final","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-12T20:00:08-07:00","id":1139821,"title":"C20 changes from backer to final","content":"Here's a thread to post changes you've found between the backer pdf that came out, and the new final version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T20:27:53-07:00","id":1139823,"title":"","content":"Index got added (19 pages)<br /> <br /> Inanime Slivers are still unleashing only<br /> <br /> Territories were not added/corrected ( would still love to know what the duchy of Violets is, and the missing territories are called)<br /> <br /> Selkies got really nerfed and have a pretty bad typo......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","user":"CameraObscura83","date":". 09-12-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T01:22:34-07:00","id":1139854,"title":"","content":"Bookmarks are fixed.<br /> <br /> -Kiths aren't nested in the Seemings bookmark and are back to being their own bookmark.<br /> <br /> -Each of the Arts now has their own bookmark.<br /> <br /> -Gallain bookmarks are in the correct order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T05:32:20-07:00","id":1139887,"title":"","content":"The typos throughout the section on Wales got fixed though! Hooray! <br /> <br /> Camera - how did selkies get nerfed? I just had a quick look and can't see that their write up has changed stats-wise? I haven't got access to the backer release just now though so I could well be misremembering...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T07:09:21-07:00","id":1139909,"title":"","content":"Seals Beauty was replaced with Seals form and the typo in tha fix is both funny and, weird","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T07:54:13-07:00","id":1139925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1139909#post1139909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seals Beauty was replaced with Seals form and the typo in tha fix is both funny and, weird</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Selkies can transform into the deep big blue or a mere sea lion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13370-urtoroth","name":"Urtoroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13370_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T08:04:23-07:00","id":1139933,"title":"","content":"So, it's looking like the Selkie birthright is the only change that would have an impact at the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 09-13-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T08:47:04-07:00","id":1139942,"title":"","content":"Ugh of course! Revoke my fannish ID card, how could I miss that. I did like that charisma boost. Giving them an extra dot and shape changing is damn beefy though. A seal might be less useful than your average pooka critter but it's also more flexible. It never costs glamour and while they need to be carrying a bottle of sea water, it doesn't get shut down entirely in the presence of mortals the way a pooka's does. All in all I can live with it. Though I agree the typo is amusing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T10:02:58-07:00","id":1139960,"title":"","content":"Well, looks like the C20 PDFs got updated again last night. Although no idea what's different about this one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T11:59:03-07:00","id":1139981,"title":"","content":"Please tell me they fixed the ridiculously stupid Pooka frailty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:37:48-07:00","id":1139997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1139981#post1139981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please tell me they fixed the ridiculously stupid Pooka frailty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's now just a straight Willpower (Difficulty 8) roll. No Willpower point expenditure at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T05:30:26-07:00","id":1140133,"title":"","content":"Mannikins are still listed as the phylla for the Kingdom of Flickers (which was just a throw-away line in the old book anyway). In fact, doesn't really seem they did much errata, just mostly fixed bookmarks and messed up other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T08:06:58-07:00","id":1140169,"title":"","content":"Did they change the Oba and River Hag Frailties? or do something about the Kiths' art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T08:54:10-07:00","id":1140187,"title":"","content":"how long till I get my collectors edition copy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:00:01-07:00","id":1140191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140187#post1140187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how long till I get my collectors edition copy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awhile still probably. According to the update, the files just got sent to the printer. That means the cover still needs to be created, pages printed and gilded, and then finally all bound together. Gilding alone is a multi-month process going by what happened with previous deluxe editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:04:53-07:00","id":1140192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140191#post1140191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Awhile still probably. According to the update, the files just got sent to the printer. That means the cover still needs to be created, pages printed and gilded, and then finally all bound together. Gilding alone is a multi-month process going by what happened with previous deluxe editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit! <br /> <br /> I was thinking along the lines of Christmass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T18:08:52-07:00","id":1140376,"title":"","content":"It's not quite the book itself, but the non-form-fillable character sheet still says &quot;NIGHGMARE.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T09:19:22-07:00","id":1140534,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda horrified by the change to selkies, now that I've had time to go on DrivethruRPG. The charisma was half the kith's appeal, while Seal Form and Ocean's Grace are largely redundant. I don't understand the choice that was made here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:49:41-07:00","id":1140552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140534#post1140534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda horrified by the change to selkies, now that I've had time to go on DrivethruRPG. The charisma was half the kith's appeal, while Seal Form and Ocean's Grace are largely redundant. I don't understand the choice that was made here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because shapeshifting is not a small thing, as powers go, and it was not represented mechanically in any way. Something had to go to make room for it. Feel free to use the first iteration if you don't mind abstracting the shapeshifting thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T21:01:18-07:00","id":1140717,"title":"","content":"Hopefully, any future books on the hsien can go to work changing the names and terms to not be in broken approximations of a source language. For now, I suppose that it can't be helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T22:00:57-07:00","id":1140723,"title":"","content":"It's a bit weird though, asking us for errata etc. and then essentially ignoring all the info that was given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T22:01:59-07:00","id":1140724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140534#post1140534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda horrified by the change to selkies, now that I've had time to go on DrivethruRPG. The charisma was half the kith's appeal, while Seal Form and Ocean's Grace are largely redundant. I don't understand the choice that was made here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just gonna keep it as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T17:10:33-07:00","id":1140930,"title":"","content":"Holy heck. That selkie change was as unnecessary as it was bad. I had players consider them before because while Ocean's Grace was pretty situational (how many adventures do you have with a significant aquatic component, really?), the other birthright was always useful.<br /> <br /> Now they have *two* super corner-case birthrights that will almost never come up unless the DM goes out of his way often, and then excludes all the other players (Who you know.. aren't good at aquatic stuff). Going to keep this the old way in our games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13398-fynikz","name":"fynikz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:17:23-07:00","id":1140940,"title":"","content":"I'm doing a cross-check of a lot of things I noted down in the backer error thread, and finding that almost none of them were corrected if it was about a mechanical inconsistency or something that just didn't work. And I don't mean &quot;suggestions on how to make the game better&quot;, but outright errors and inconsistencies. That's... really disheartening for the effort put in double checking the book. Looks like it's time for a lot of house rules.<br /> <br /> For example, the Invoking the Wyrd section still just states &quot;The changeling can soak lethal damage while invoking the Wyrd.&quot; and the combat example specifically states &quot;because Call<br /> the Wyrd causes the bullet\u2019s damage to be treated as chimerical...&quot; and &quot;...and so reduces the total damage from 4 health levels to 1 health level of lethal chimerical damage.&quot; Even though Invoking the Wyrd mentions nothing about converting damage types (which makes a big difference for healing times).<br /> <br /> Greatswords are still difficulty 5 and STR+6 lethal. Even though they are difficulty 7 in every other X20 property and deal more damage at STR+6 than any other weapon in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13398-fynikz","name":"fynikz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T20:33:40-07:00","id":1140964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fynikz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140930#post1140930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy heck. That selkie change was as unnecessary as it was bad. I had players consider them before because while Ocean's Grace was pretty situational (how many adventures do you have with a significant aquatic component, really?), the other birthright was always useful.<br /> <br /> Now they have *two* super corner-case birthrights that will almost never come up unless the DM goes out of his way often, and then excludes all the other players (Who you know.. aren't good at aquatic stuff). Going to keep this the old way in our games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I were playing a selkie, I'd expect the game to be set somewhere near an ocean. Conversely, if the Storyteller is setting their game in Des Moines, I think I'd know better than to play a selkie (or, at least, I'd expect not to get much use out of my seal-related abilities). <br /> <br /> I already explained the thinking behind the change. Sorry if it doesn't work for you. Fair cop about the Invoking the Wyrd; I missed it in the combat example, evidently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T00:59:43-07:00","id":1141001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140964#post1140964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were playing a selkie, I'd expect the game to be set somewhere near an ocean. Conversely, if the Storyteller is setting their game in Des Moines, I think I'd know better than to play a selkie (or, at least, I'd expect not to get much use out of my seal-related abilities).</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet mechanically, nothing is stopping a selkie from leaving the ocean or the coastline.<br /> <br /> Looking over their rules, there's nothing there saying a selkie HAS to be near the sea. Sure, they won't be able to use their Seal Form, but they still have Ocean's Grace. And looking at the RAW text, it applies to their human form and works in all types of water, not just seawater. Their old Frailty, &quot;Longing of the Ocean Shore&quot; (aka the one that would give a selkie Banality points every day they were away from the sea) wasn't carried over into C20. And thus far, no one seems to miss its' absence.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'd be extremely confused if a player wanted to play a selkie when a chronicle is set in the middle of the Gobi Desert...but technically there are no mechanics that stops that player from making that selkie in such a location.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, my personal hotfix would be to just combine Seal Form and Ocean's Grace into one Birthright. Something like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ocean\u2019s Grace</b>:<br /> Selkies can take the form of a seal or sea lion at will. They must be wrapped in their seal coat and touching (though not necessarily immersed) in sea water for this to occur. Additionally, Selkies reduce the difficulty for all rolls involving Dexterity by two while in the water. This applies either in human or seal form. Because of that, they can never botch a Swimming roll. Finally, selkies can hold their breath for hours, whether in water or out of it. </div> </div> </div>And then just use Seal's Beauty wholesale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 09-17-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T07:12:12-07:00","id":1141057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141001#post1141001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet mechanically, nothing is stopping a selkie from leaving the ocean or the coastline.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, of course there's not. Why would there be? <br /> <br /> I don't think it's a controversial notion to say that the choices players make during chargen should influence the setting of the game, or that, depending on how you're doing it, the setting that the Storyteller has put forth should guide chargen choices. That's one of the reasons the example of character creation in C20 is written the way it is - it's not one player creating a character in a vacuum or even with just the ST, it's a group creating characters and we're just zeroing in on one. <br /> <br /> Kithain get two Birthrights and one Frailty. One thing we tried to do was smooth those out, because OWoD mechanics liked to try and stack multiple things under one header and I always found it confusing. One example: Selkies, so much of their power and identity wrapped up in being able to change into a seal, but no mechanical support for that. Why? <br /> <br /> Understand, I'm not saying your fix is wrong. I'm just explaining the thinking from my perspective as the designer. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:14:14-07:00","id":1141513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140964#post1140964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I were playing a selkie, I'd expect the game to be set somewhere near an ocean. Conversely, if the Storyteller is setting their game in Des Moines, I think I'd know better than to play a selkie (or, at least, I'd expect not to get much use out of my seal-related abilities).<br /> <br /> I already explained the thinking behind the change. Sorry if it doesn't work for you. Fair cop about the Invoking the Wyrd; I missed it in the combat example, evidently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for the hostile tone (and it's cool the developers show up here), this was coming right after my selkie player basically decided to redo his character as a different kith due to the changes.<br /> <br /> The issue with the seal birthright to me is it feels like over-specialization and that it doesn't add much else to the character. For instance, a pooka who turns into a tiger gains combat abilities, as well as some athletics/climbing abilities. A pooka who turns into a ferret (like our intro character Tisket-von-Tasket) gains the ability to masquerade as a pet, infiltrate small, hard to reach places, etc (as she does in the intro). An alleycat pooka is unlikely to get much attention paid to him in a city while he overhears a conversation.<br /> <br /> On top of this, all pooka have their secondary ability, Confidante for social situations. Satyrs have a stamina (combat and athletics) ability and a social ability (gift of pan).<br /> <br /> But turning into a seal mostly grants you bonuses in the aquatic realm, and it feels like those are pretty much all covered under Ocean's Grace already - you're more agile in the water, can hold your breathe basically forever, etc. Being able to turn into a seal doesn't feel like it extends your abilities beyond things you could already do under Ocean's Grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13398-fynikz","name":"fynikz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:01:45-07:00","id":1141605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141057#post1141057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's a controversial notion to say that the choices players make during chargen should influence the setting of the game, or that, depending on how you're doing it, the setting that the Storyteller has put forth should guide chargen choices. That's one of the reasons the example of character creation in C20 is written the way it is - it's not one player creating a character in a vacuum or even with just the ST, it's a group creating characters and we're just zeroing in on one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be fine...for Gallain. <br /> <br /> My reading of the kiths as presented in C20 as a whole is that the the core Kithain are supposed to be the most broad and accessible as player options: the options that are the most versatile and adaptable to any kind of story you want to tell. Sure, officially in-story the Kithan are supposed to be indicative of Euro-American mythology and culture, but I personally find the archetypes they represent to be flexible enough that you could accommodate them in any place in the world, especially if your players and ST don't want want to do a full conversion of making new kiths from the ground up with their own mechanical sub-systems.<br /> <br /> For instance, I find Japan's historic roots in feudalism and imperialism to be a pretty close mapping to the Euro-feudalism, that making a palette swap of the Kithain to be a fairly simple affair. Trolls as Oni, anyone? <br /> <br /> When you start getting to the more offshoot and weirder options like the Bloodlines in Vampire, the Fera in Werewolf, the Crafts/Disparates in Mage, and in the case of Changeling, the Gallain, THAT'S when you start needing to consider doing more niche and specific stories for chronicles, because the Gallain in of themselves are more niche with more specific concepts behind him. I have full expectations of a Hsien game being completely different from a game that's primarily of the Kithain. <br /> <br /> That shouldn't be something that's in the core Kithain, including the selkies. <br /> <br /> Selkies should be as broad and adaptable as the other Kithain to any of the type of chronicles in a Changeling. To do otherwise makes them stick out...and not in a good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:16:41-07:00","id":1141610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141605#post1141605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be fine...for Gallain. <br /> <br /> My reading of the kiths as presented in C20 as a whole is that the the core Kithain are supposed to be the most broad and accessible as player options: the options that are the most versatile and adaptable to any kind of story you want to tell. Sure, officially in-story the Kithan are supposed to be indicative of Euro-American mythology and culture, but I personally find the archetypes they represent to be flexible enough that you could accommodate them in any place in the world, especially if your players and ST don't want want to do a full conversion of making new kiths from the ground up with their own mechanical sub-systems.<br /> <br /> For instance, I find Japan's historic roots in feudalism and imperialism to be a pretty close mapping to the Euro-feudalism, that making a palette swap of the Kithain to be a fairly simple affair. Trolls as Oni, anyone? <br /> <br /> When you start getting to the more offshoot and weirder options like the Bloodlines in Vampire, the Fera in Werewolf, the Crafts/Disparates in Mage, and in the case of Changeling, the Gallain, THAT'S when you start needing to consider doing more niche and specific stories for chronicles, because the Gallain in of themselves are more niche with more specific concepts behind him. I have full expectations of a Hsien game being completely different from a game that's primarily of the Kithain. <br /> <br /> That shouldn't be something that's in the core Kithain, including the selkies. <br /> <br /> Selkies should be as broad and adaptable as the other Kithain to any of the type of chronicles in a Changeling. To do otherwise makes them stick out...and not in a good way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your issue there are bigger problems than selkies. You pretty much can't have a Title 5 Gwydion sidhe and an Unseelie redcap in the same motley either, at least not without making it a much bigger deal than having the game set on the coast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T20:20:20-07:00","id":1141635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141610#post1141610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's your issue there are bigger problems than selkies. You pretty much can't have a Title 5 Gwydion sidhe and an Unseelie redcap in the same motley either, at least not without making it a much bigger deal than having the game set on the coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and yet nothing mechanically in the book says that you neither need to or absolutely can't have a Title 5 Gwydion sidhe and Unseelie redcap at the same time in the same motley? Especially in C20 where it's as lenient as its ever been on mixed Courts and mixed Houses motleys?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're getting at here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 09-18-2017, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:17:06-07:00","id":1141698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141605#post1141605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trolls as Oni, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yah, here!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T16:32:29-07:00","id":1141932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1140552#post1140552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because shapeshifting is not a small thing, as powers go, and it was not represented mechanically in any way. Something had to go to make room for it. Feel free to use the first iteration if you don't mind abstracting the shapeshifting thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying Ocean's grace is a mechanical representation of Seal Form? Instead of having 2 redundant abilities, they have 1 in 2 parts? Or am I completely misunderstanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 09-19-2017, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T16:18:50-07:00","id":1142332,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to agree on the matter of Selkies; I've already made the changes to my game to re-install Seal's Beauty. Appearance doesn't come up much; Charisma does. I run a game set beside the ocean and I still feel that this change is too niche-oriented and could have been folded into Ocean's Grace. There just aren't a lot of uses for their Birthrights as written outside of the water, and that is still where most of the action takes place. And as written in the new version, it IS niche; you even have to be immersed in ocean water for it to work, so there's not even a chance of surprising somebody by having a demure woman turn into a gargantuan seal and flopping onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","user":"Windthin","date":". 09-20-2017, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T06:35:20-07:00","id":1142482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1142332#post1142332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to agree on the matter of Selkies; I've already made the changes to my game to re-install Seal's Beauty. Appearance doesn't come up much; Charisma does. I run a game set beside the ocean and I still feel that this change is too niche-oriented and could have been folded into Ocean's Grace. There just aren't a lot of uses for their Birthrights as written outside of the water, and that is still where most of the action takes place. And as written in the new version, it IS niche; you even have to be immersed in ocean water for it to work, so there's not even a chance of surprising somebody by having a demure woman turn into a gargantuan seal and flopping onto them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with you on some of that but Selkies don't have to be immersed in seawater only touching and the rulebook specifically points that out. &quot; touching (though not necessarily immersed) in seawater for this to occur&quot; pp105","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T15:46:42-07:00","id":1143064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1141605#post1141605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For instance, I find Japan's historic roots in feudalism and imperialism to be a pretty close mapping to the Euro-feudalism, that making a palette swap of the Kithain to be a fairly simple affair. Trolls as Oni, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>For some of them, but didn't the last thread to go into this mention that they would fall into a case of &quot;looks like a troll, acts like a rock giant?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T23:13:19-07:00","id":1143157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143064#post1143064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some of them, but didn't the last thread to go into this mention that they would fall into a case of &quot;looks like a troll, acts like a rock giant?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my suggestion. Though Conversely I wouldn't question someone using a Pooka to run a Tanuki or Kitsune. Shapeshifting Animal trickster is what I'd say a solid universal concept. Same with &quot;small helper guy&quot; and &quot;Crazy twisted Crafter&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T02:56:50-07:00","id":1143185,"title":"","content":"Yikes! The Selkies nerf was an awful and unnecessary one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T14:25:58-07:00","id":1143321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143064#post1143064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some of them, but didn't the last thread to go into this mention that they would fall into a case of &quot;looks like a troll, acts like a rock giant?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It's not a perfect mapping, to be sure, but with a little tweaking that could be taken care of.<br /> <br /> (although to be perfectly frank: the CtD Trolls have almost no resemblance to actual trolls from myth. Ain't nothing in the original myths that say trolls are honorable, oath-bound warriors)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143157#post1143157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my suggestion. Though Conversely I wouldn't question someone using a Pooka to run a Tanuki or Kitsune. Shapeshifting Animal trickster is what I'd say a solid universal concept. Same with &quot;small helper guy&quot; and &quot;Crazy twisted Crafter&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a bit of the other Kiths one could make them just generic concepts that you could re-skin to fit the regions and culture. I could say the same for &quot;ethereal leader&quot; or &quot;slimy creatures in the dark that know Things&quot;<br /> <br /> I personally subscribe to the interpretation that the Dreaming is universal and everywhere, it's just that the various changelings interpret it and their relationship to the Dreaming. Doesn't matter if we're all separated by distance, language, or culture: we are all human, and we all dream the same dreams.<br /> <br /> So therefore it would stand to reason the changelings across the world would bear some similarities to each other.<br /> <br /> (weirdness of the Hsien aside)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T19:27:38-07:00","id":1143387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143321#post1143321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. It's not a perfect mapping, to be sure, but with a little tweaking that could be taken care of.<br /> <br /> (although to be perfectly frank: the CtD Trolls have almost no resemblance to actual trolls from myth. Ain't nothing in the original myths that say trolls are honorable, oath-bound warriors)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if i want to play an Oni I want to be a violent punchy guy who uses honor to keep myself in check, not someone who's power comes from Honor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite a bit of the other Kiths one could make them just generic concepts that you could re-skin to fit the regions and culture. I could say the same for &quot;ethereal leader&quot; or &quot;slimy creatures in the dark that know Things&quot;<br /> <br /> I personally subscribe to the interpretation that the Dreaming is universal and everywhere, it's just that the various changelings interpret it and their relationship to the Dreaming. Doesn't matter if we're all separated by distance, language, or culture: we are all human, and we all dream the same dreams.<br /> <br /> So therefore it would stand to reason the changelings across the world would bear some similarities to each other.<br /> <br /> (weirdness of the Hsien aside) </div> </div> </div>some are easier to reskin than others, and some work really fucking hard to not be all that reskinable...(Sidhe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T06:51:07-07:00","id":1146321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143387#post1143387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if i want to play an Oni I want to be a violent punchy guy who uses honor to keep myself in check, not someone who's power comes from Honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically, you'd just play with their Frailty a bit and mythology. Otherwise, they are the same big old Trolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1143387#post1143387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and some work really fucking hard to not be all that reskinable...(Sidhe)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T15:50:03-07:00","id":1146466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146321#post1146321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically, you'd just play with their Frailty a bit and mythology. Otherwise, they are the same big old Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rock Giants exist! I Think Oni are Oni. They might mechanically and visually share some stuff with Trolls but Oni are Oni. Not Trolls, not Ogres not Rock Giants.<br /> <br /> Trolls are Giant Honorable guys. Oni are Giant angry Guys. Rock Giants, Oni, Cyclopses I could see as sort of a base thing, but trolls represent a different archtype.<br /> <br /> I don't have the same issue with KItsune/Tanuki/etc are Pooka because I think Pooka hits on the same archetype. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you think so? </div> </div> </div>How many Houses are Celtic? You have a token handful that aren't. Along with stuff like Oba so there's presenation that they are universal like Pooka but potentially also just culturally specific imperialists from Celtlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T20:23:01-07:00","id":1146545,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146466#post1146466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rock Giants exist! I Think Oni are Oni. They might mechanically and visually share some stuff with Trolls but Oni are Oni. Not Trolls, not Ogres not Rock Giants.<br /> <br /> Trolls are Giant Honorable guys. Oni are Giant angry Guys. Rock Giants, Oni, Cyclopses I could see as sort of a base thing, but trolls represent a different archtype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ogres and Trolls, at least in earlier editions is.. was the same things. Orges are the anrgy ones. The Trolls without morals. Basically, they are almost, like - ??? (you have three guesses). Like, I get, that different cultures produce different creatures and morals. But consider Hercules for a moment. Or &quot;real&quot; Trolls from legends. Those are all a different interpretations, different stories, different happy and unhappy endings of the same myth, if we consider Dreaming as origin point of all stories, of entire universe, maybe. And stories about &quot;trolls&quot; and &quot;brutes&quot; usually touch upon strength, folly, madness and responsibility. How those stories are resolved, what makes Trolls - Trolls, and Oni - Oni. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146466#post1146466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Houses are Celtic? You have a token handful that aren't. Along with stuff like Oba so there's presenation that they are universal like Pooka but potentially also just culturally specific imperialists from Celtlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main thing of Sidhe is being awe-inspiring, beautiful and noble. Which makes them pretty damn portable and reskinable.<br /> <br /> (Even elven ears are not requirement, considering how a new creative invention those are)<br /> <br /> Considering, that non-Celtic Houses exist, that gives you licence to make stuff up, like maybe they don't have Houses in the traditional sense in the Land of the Rising Sun.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd ditch all regional Houses and allow far-off land &quot;Sidhe&quot; to have their own House/Dynastic/Clan systems, instead. But Birthrights/Frailties seem to be pretty universal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T21:02:46-07:00","id":1146556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146545#post1146545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOgres and Trolls, at least in earlier editions is.. was the same things. Orges are the anrgy ones. The Trolls without morals. Basically, they are almost, like - ??? (you have three guesses). Like, I get, that different cultures produce different creatures and morals. But consider Hercules for a moment. Or &quot;real&quot; Trolls from legends. Those are all a different interpretations, different stories, different happy and unhappy endings of the same myth, if we consider Dreaming as origin point of all stories, of entire universe, maybe. And stories about &quot;trolls&quot; and &quot;brutes&quot; usually touch upon strength, folly, madness and responsibility. How those stories are resolved, what makes Trolls - Trolls, and Oni - Oni.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think they touch upon the same story. That's what I am saying. Troll(Even it it doesn't cover mythic trolls) is big honorable guy who has control of themselves. Hercules, Cyclopes, Onis, Rock Giants are a different story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the main thing of Sidhe is being awe-inspiring, beautiful and noble. Which makes them pretty damn portable and reskinable.<br /> <br /> (Even elven ears are not requirement, considering how a new creative invention those are)<br /> <br /> Considering, that non-Celtic Houses exist, that gives you licence to make stuff up, like maybe they don't have Houses in the traditional sense in the Land of the Rising Sun.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd ditch all regional Houses and allow far-off land &quot;Sidhe&quot; to have their own House/Dynastic/Clan systems, instead. But Birthrights/Frailties seem to be pretty universal. </div> </div> </div>I find the sidhe to be reskinable in spite of what they try to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T21:48:42-07:00","id":1146567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146556#post1146556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they touch upon the same story. That's what I am saying. Troll(Even it it doesn't cover mythic trolls) is big honorable guy who has control of themselves. Hercules, Cyclopes, Onis, Rock Giants are a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Whatever you say, man. <br /> <br /> Have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T08:28:07-07:00","id":1146680,"title":"","content":"Um, have you *read* the Herakles myths? Nothing about him was about self control, or even honour really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T10:32:22-07:00","id":1146722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146680#post1146680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, have you *read* the Herakles myths? Nothing about him was about self control, or even honour really.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why he's in the category with Oni and Rock Giants. Rage and destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T12:02:18-07:00","id":1146749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139821-c20-changes-from-backer-to-final?p=1146680#post1146680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, have you *read* the Herakles myths? Nothing about him was about self control, or even honour really.</div> </div> </div> </div>He got punished with a public servitude for the lack of self-restraint, according to the myths. Whether it did taught him any good life lessons is up to debate, but he didn't commit most of his heroic deeds for a fun of it. Some were so demeaning, that he had to cheat them with a technicality, like Stables of Augeius.<br /> <br /> And later he got cursed with madness, which turned his strength against him, robbing him of his family, children.<br /> <br /> It's not about Heracles, practicing a lot of self-restraint and patience, Peter Parker-style, but rather a cautionary tale about society being able to force you to pay your dues for (killing a serviceable artist) being selfish dick and gods being able to screw with you in a worst way imaginable, despite you having crazy superpowers. And how lack of self-restraint, chosen or inflicted upon you, ultimately a bad thing. Unless you're a god or something.<br /> <br /> My interpretation. Not an ancient greek myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 10-04-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}